      "side": 1,
      "message": "mm/slab.h in 5.10:\nstruct track {\n        unsigned long addr;     /* Called from address */\n#ifdef CONFIG_STACKTRACE\n        unsigned long addrs[TRACK_ADDRS_COUNT]; /* Called from address */\n#endif\n        int cpu;                /* Was running on cpu */\n        int pid;                /* Pid context */\n        unsigned long when;     /* When did the operation occur */\n#ifdef CONFIG_STACKTRACE\n        ANDROID_OEM_DATA(1);\n#endif\n};\nIn 5.10, we added ANDROID_OEM_DATA in struct track to record hash value. And it is not included in 5.15. As it is not available to modify struct anymore, we will reuse the \u0027track-\u003ewhen\u0027 to save hash, because the timestamp is not important for us. So we must move the hook down to overwrite the original \u0027track-\u003ewhen\u0027 assignment.",
